**Hand off**: `{{ skill_prefix }}pipelex-inputs` prepares sample inputs, or test files with planted facts, then `{{ skill_prefix }}pipelex-run` runs the method, and `{{ skill_prefix }}pipelex-lab` writes answer keys and scores the runs; `{{ skill_prefix }}pipelex-catalog` saves it under an `mt_…` id; `{{ skill_prefix }}pipelex-integrate` wires it into a codebase (a `package.json` or a `pyproject.toml`), and with neither, `{{ skill_prefix }}pipelex-scaffold` creates an app around it.
